# Code owners are requested for review automatically on every pull request.
#
# One maintainer today, so a catch-all is honest: naming per-directory owners
# would imply a review rota that does not exist. The specific entries below are
# not narrower ownership — they mark the files where a wrong change is expensive
# and silent, so that a future co-maintainer inherits the emphasis rather than
# having to rediscover it.

*                                   @guidoiaquinti

# The recorded limactl contract. Everything in internal/lima is written against
# it, and a change here that is not verified against a real Lima invalidates the
# fake, the fixtures and the acceptance suite at once.
/docs/development/lima-cli-contract.md  @guidoiaquinti
/internal/testutil/                     @guidoiaquinti

# Release and CI plumbing. A mistake here is not caught by any test: it either
# ships a broken artifact or weakens the workflow permissions model.
/.github/workflows/                 @guidoiaquinti
/.goreleaser.yml                    @guidoiaquinti
/terraform-registry-manifest.json   @guidoiaquinti

# The documentation source. docs/ is generated from here, so a change to
# templates/ is what actually reaches the Terraform Registry — and a pull
# request touching docs/ without touching templates/ is almost certainly a hand
# edit that the next `make docs` will revert.
/templates/                         @guidoiaquinti
/docs/                              @guidoiaquinti
